course: dictionary
lesson: 9658
title: Subordinate clauses
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Subordinate means lower or less important. In grammar, a subordinate clause is a group of words that has a verb but cannot stand alone. «When the bell rings» has a verb, but it does not finish a thought, so it needs a main clause to lean on.
explain: A main clause makes sense on its own: «The dog barked.» Add a subordinate clause and you get «When the postman came, the dog barked.» The clause «When the postman came» depends on the main clause to make full sense.
explain: Words such as because, although, when, if and while often start subordinate clauses. When the subordinate clause comes first, put a comma after it. At work, a subordinate is a person with a lower rank who takes orders from a boss.
fact: Subordinate has three meanings: in grammar, a clause that leans on a main clause; at work, a person of lower rank; and, formally, less important than something else.
fact: A subordinate clause has a verb but cannot stand alone. It depends on a main clause.
fact: Subordinate clauses usually start with words like because, when, if, although, while, after, before, until, since or as.
fact: In «Although it was cold, we went out», the subordinate clause is «Although it was cold» and the main clause is «we went out».
fact: When a subordinate clause comes first, a comma follows it. When it comes second, usually no comma is needed.
exercise: In «Although it was cold, we went out», which part is the subordinate clause? | Although | we went out | *Although it was cold | it was cold, we
exercise: Which group of words can stand alone as a sentence? | when the postman came | because it was raining | *The dog barked. | although the sun shone
exercise: Which word starts the subordinate clause in «We stayed inside because it rained»? | *because | We | stayed | inside
test: Which sentence has a subordinate clause that comes first and needs a comma? | Mum bought bread and milk. | The cat slept on the mat. | We played outside. | *When the bell rang, the class stood up.
test: At work, what does subordinate mean? | A person who never works | *A person with a lower rank who takes orders | A boss who gives orders | A clause with a comma
exam: In grammar, a subordinate clause is one that | *has a verb but cannot stand alone | can stand alone as a full sentence | is always longer than a main clause | never has a verb
